22 0 obj
<< /A 215 0 R /Alt (Three-panel figure displaying correlation matrices as colored dot plots for various health, psychiatric, and emotional outcomes. Panel a shows associations between early bleeding outcomes and four gynecological conditions; panel b depicts associations with metabolic and cardiovascular health measures; panel c illustrates associations with psychiatric disorders and emotional traits. Dot size and blue to red color scale indicate strength and direction of correlation, with asterisks representing statistical significance. X-axes list outcomes, and Y-axes list bleeding groups, with separate rows for both sexes, females, and males. Color key bar appears below each panel for correlation coefficients.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 216 0 R /Alt (Graphic showing human chromosomes labeled one to twenty-two with colored icons marking specific loci linked to psychiatric, gynecological, and cardiometabolic conditions. A legend at the bottom defines each color and shape corresponding to specific condition pairings. Chromosomes are vertically oriented with dark and light bands. Colored circles, squares, and triangles correspond to disorders such as ADHD, ASD, PTSD, MDD, endometriosis, and cardiometabolic traits, with some chromosomes having multiple loci indicated for different conditions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 217 0 R /Alt (Manhattan plot showing association results for single nucleotide polymorphisms on chromosome 15. Y-axis displays negative log base ten p-values and the X-axis shows chromosomal position. Dots are colored by linkage disequilibrium value, with rs45457497 labeled prominently. Multiple genes including CASC5, RAD51-AS1, RAD51, RMDN3, GCHFR, DNAJC17, and C15orf62 are annotated below. A color key for r-squared values and recombination rate in centiMorgans per megabase is included.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 218 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot illustrating single nucleotide polymorphisms \(SNPs\) on chromosome eleven, with dot colors indicating linkage disequilibrium \(r²\) values. The y-axis shows negative log ten p-values, the x-axis shows position in megabases, and the right y-axis indicates recombination rates in centimorgans per megabase. SNP rs2452681 is highlighted at the top, and gene regions are displayed below the plot with labeled gene symbols.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 219 0 R /Alt (Three-panel scientific figure comparing genetic association data for ADHD and EBA. Left panel: scatter plot of -log10\(P\) values for ADHD \(y-axis\) and EBA \(x-axis\) with a labeled variant rs45457497 as a purple diamond. Top right: EBA association Manhattan plot for chromosome fifteen with rs45457497 labeled. Bottom right: ADHD association Manhattan plot for the same region with rs45457497 labeled. Points are colored by significance.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 220 0 R /Alt (Three scatterplots displaying genetic association data are shown. The left plot compares EBA and BIP negative log10 p-values, highlighting point rs2452681 in purple. The two right panels show local association signals across chromosome 11 positions for EBA \(top\) and BIP \(bottom\), again highlighting rs2452681. Dots are color-coded by significance or data type, demonstrating regional association patterns.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
